# rule.forbid.handrolled-search-over-scarce-resources

never hand-write a search over combinations of scarce resources — instructors × slots × boards, drivers × routes, rooms × shifts. it is operations research (define.software-domain-taxonomy); nested loops that try combinations blow up on a real roster and miss the best answer
smell: nested loops over two or more resource sets · a greedy "first fit" pass with retries · a comment like "try the next instructor if this one is full"
cure: declare the formulation — variables, constraints, objective — and hand it to a solver (linear, integer, constraint). the formulation reads as the domain's rules; the solver finds the answer
enforcement: hand-written search over combinations of scarce resources = blocker
